wn  number four tywin lannister you want to  talk about ways to go down  probably the most embarrassing one that  we've seen on this show but  you know what he earned those crossbow  bolts boy did he ever  you know i've mentioned about some of  these characters just the sense of  authority you have to them  this guy not only had a sense of  authority he had a sense of  menace to him and not necessarily a  physical madness like he was gonna  personally bash your head in but  you just felt from his very first scene  his very first time talking to anybody  and  if you don't remember it was him laying  the verbal smackdown on his son  the son he liked at that and just how  commanding the guy is i mean  you do not question this is a man in  complete  and total control of his immediate  surroundings and the situation going on  he knows what's what and he knows how to  get  all the pieces moved exactly where he  wants them to be  and yet despite this very sort of arch  construction he still felt very human  and you did get bits of emotion and bits  of  humanity out of him as the thing went  along really a strength of  charles dance's performance number three  oberyn martell  we'll get to how he ended up in a minute  but man  pure charm the instant he  showed up he kind of has that inigo  montoya flavor to him from the princess  bride i'm not just saying that because  of the accent  he has that swagger that charm but that  obsessive need for revenge at the same  time  like that's that's a hell of a  combination and it works terrifically  here i mean the guy just  oozes charm and appeal and sex but  then you see him start to talk about his  desire for revenge against the  lannisters and against the mountain  you're like  oh okay this guy is not all about  pleasure he is about some very serious  stuff too  and then of course we can't talk about  oberyn without talking about that fight  and the way he died oh my god  i mean that that death just  hurt to watch it hurt because i